<details class="outline" id="outline">
<summary>Read as an outline</summary>
<p>Only what the tests need.</p>
<section class="t-word">
<h2>The Word</h2>
<p>A reason “that orders” the world.</p>
<ol>
<li><span class="thread">The Word</span> <a href="#k-ben">Ben of Somewhere</a> <b>adapts</b> <a href="#k-ana">Ana</a> (<cite>Ben 1.1</cite>): “In the beginning.”</li>
<li><span class="thread">The Word</span> <a href="#k-cal">Cal</a> <b>quotes</b> <a href="#k-ben">Ben of Somewhere</a> (<cite>Cal 2</cite>): “As Ben said.”</li>
</ol>
</section>
<section class="t-law">
<h2>The law</h2>
<p>A law written on the heart.</p>
<ol>
<li><span class="thread">The law</span> <a href="#k-dee">Dee</a> <b>rejects</b> <a href="#k-ana">Ana</a> (<cite>Dee 3</cite>): Dee argues against Ana.</li>
<li><span class="thread">The law</span> <a href="#k-dee">Dee</a> <b>may draw on</b> <a href="#k-cal">Cal</a> (<cite>Dee 4</cite>): Whether Dee knew Cal is argued.</li>
</ol>
</section>
